KW  - modeling
KW  - ALGORITHMS
AB  - Floods cause severe global damage, demanding smarter, data-driven solutions. Geospatial Artificial Intelligence (GeoAI) integrated with Generative Pre-trained Transformers (GPT) is advancing flood disaster management through intelligent automation, data fusion, and adaptive geospatial analysis. This study systematically reviews 130 selected papers from a large initial pool using the Preferred Reporting Items for Systematic Reviews and Meta-Analyses (PRISMA) framework, providing a comprehensive assessment of methodologies and technologies in flood mapping and hydrological modeling. A quantitative synthesis shows that approximately 45-50% of studies employ machine learning ensembles, 25-30% deep learning models, 18-22% physically based approaches, and only 3-5% explore GPT-based techniques. Based on these insights, FloodMapGPT is introduced as a conceptual, forward-looking framework to demonstrate how GeoAI and GPT technologies can be systematically integrated into future flood-mapping and decision-support systems. The framework enables natural language interaction with geospatial data, facilitating automated report generation and flood analysis. Furthermore, this study outlines key opportunities, challenges, and future research directions, emphasizing the need to adapt GPT for spatial reasoning and geospatial intelligence to support next-generation flood management systems.
