AB  - This perspective discussed issues on the pre-training and downstream tasks and applications of Urban Mobility Foundation Models (UMFMs). Specifically, we need to consider various mobility data modality and effective representation approaches, ensuring data transparency and model interpretability, addressing geographical scale, zoning, biases, spatiotemporal sampling strategies, location data and geo-privacy issues. In addition, human centered perspectives and sense of place and community need to be considered when applying UMFMs in various downstream tasks to support urban planing, design, decision making and governance.
