AB  - Cyclists often receive route suggestions that prioritize speed over comfort or safety. Popular navigation tools tend to favor busy roads, ignoring preferences for quieter, more scenic, or amenity-rich paths. We introduce Biker Buddy (BB), a conversational route planner powered by Large Language Models (LLMs) and geospatial context compression.
   BB allows users to interact naturally when planning bike routes, refining suggestions in real-time based on individual needs-such as avoiding traffic, unpaved roads, or stopping at specific points of interest. To stay within LLM context limits, BB compresses map data intelligently and integrates with Open Source Routing Machine (OSRM) for baseline routing.
   Our early results show that BB can generate safer, more personalized bike routes while supporting dynamic conversation. BB offers a flexible, human-centered approach to map-based AI navigation.
