AB  - Accurate representation of geometric shapes and structures plays a pivotal role in facilitating the recognition and segmentation of point clouds, particularly in remote sensing applications involving irregular, sparse, and large-scale data. Graph neural networks (GNNs) are a widely used method for encoding geometric relationships among points through edge operators within a latent space projection. However, prevailing graph operators of point cloud within GNNs have not been explicitly tailored to incorporate directional gradient operations, which are crucial for capturing essential structural information especially in challenging cases. To address this, we introduce a novel graph convolution operator, termed the Point Gradient (PointGrad) operator. PointGrad is carefully designed to effectively capture directional tensor gradients of individual points, subsequently mapping them into a high-dimensional, multiscale tensor space. The PointGrad operator adaptively encodes diverse orders of partial derivatives, thereby more completely encapsulating multiscale geometric shape details and curvature characteristics. Integrating the PointGrad operator into graph convolutions over distributed, irregular point sets helps capture key surface structure properties within the point cloud across varying spatial and feature scales to empower efficient learning. Stacking of PointGrad operators leads to a new family of deep networks that we call PointGradNet. Experimental results demonstrate the effectiveness and generalization of the proposed PointGrad operator across a range of benchmark datasets varying in spatial scale, data sources, and task granularities, including urban scene airborne LiDAR point cloud segmentation, indoor scene semantic segmentation, and object part segmentation. Experiments on remote sensing benchmarks, including the IEEE DFT4 and COU2014 LiDAR datasets, demonstrate that PointGrad significantly improves segmentation accuracy and robustness in complex geospatial environments, providing a powerful, interpretable tool for scene understanding in Earth observation and GeoAI. Code is available at https://github.com/CIVA-Lab/PointGradNet
